We currently have a vacancy for a Test Automation Engineer fluent in English, to offer his/her services as an expert remotely (within EU) . In the context of the first assignment, the successful candidate will be integrated in the Development team of the company that will closely cooperate with a major client’s IT team.

Tasks: 

- Define test automation approaches and patterns fit for products in scope (UI, backend and data driven);
- Create test automation frameworks, patterns which support are reliable, provide fast feedback and easy to maintain test suites;
- Create and review test cases and test automation suites to efficiently increase test coverage;
- Mentor test engineers in understanding and applying test automation frameworks, patterns when creating automated tests; 
- Drive proof of concepts and adoption of test automation frameworks and patterns.

Requirements 

- University degree in IT combined with relevant IT professional experience of at least 5 years;
- Minimum 5 years of experience in testing automation patterns and frameworks (UI, backend and data driven); 
- Experience (Java, Java/TypeScript, python preferred) and common automation tools like Tosca, Playwright, Selenium and Appium;
- Experience in test automation framework creation and maintenance;
- Experience in test automation suite creation and maintenance;
- Experience in embedding automated test suites as part of CI/CD pipelines and leveraging the results as quality and promotion gates;
- Experience in integration of test automation suite results into test management tools; 
- Experience in complex, enterprise system integration; 
- Experience in agile software development and testing methodologies; 
- Excellent command of the English language.
Benefits 

If you are seeking a career in an exciting and dynamic company, where you will offer your services as part of a team of a major European Institution, operating in an international, multilingual and multicultural environment where you can expect real chances to make a difference, please send us your detailed CV in English, quoting reference: (ST/TAE/10/2026). 

We offer a competitive remuneration (either on contract basis or remuneration with full benefits package), based on qualifications and experience. All applications will be treated as confidential. 

You may also consider all our other open vacancies by visiting the career section of our web site ( www.eurodyn.com) and follow us on Twitter (@EURODYN_Careers) and LinkedIn. 

